From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vigaz <pudimdebacon3@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:51:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Fix ConcurrentModificationException crashing
 system_server

Two different locks were guarding the same mutable state (mControls):
most of this class synchronizes on the explicit mLock object, but
executeRefreshControls() and fetchControlsList() used method-level
synchronized instead, which locks on `this` - a different monitor. That
let two threads race through refreshControlsLocked()'s
mControls.clear()/put() loop at the same time, corrupting the ArrayMap.

Crashed live on device: changing the GPU governor in Kernel Manager
(SettingsObserver.onChange -> handleSettingChanged -> applyControlUpdate,
which does hold mLock) raced against a concurrent getControls() call
(fetchControlsList, which didn't), producing

  java.util.ConcurrentModificationException
      at android.util.ArrayMap.put(ArrayMap.java:606)
      at AxKernelManagerService.refreshControlsLocked(...:198)
      at AxKernelManagerService.applyControlUpdate(...:174)
      at AxKernelManagerService.handleSettingChanged(...:154)

and took system_server down with it (a full framework restart, felt as
a slow "soft reboot"). Pre-existing race, but far more likely to fire
now that GPU controls actually apply and AxDiagnostics polls this
service more (both landed earlier today).

Switches both methods to synchronize on mLock like the rest of the
class already does, so all five entry points touching mControls share
one consistent lock.

Change-Id: If4dc20ef735cbde37cb2f2e517d5ec972c68f629
---
 .../server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java      | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java b/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java
index 37fd4f4..1188d39 100644
--- a/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java
+++ b/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java
@@ -185,8 +185,10 @@ public final class AxKernelManagerService {
         }
     }
 
-    private synchronized void executeRefreshControls() {
-        refreshControlsLocked();
+    private void executeRefreshControls() {
+        synchronized (mLock) {
+            refreshControlsLocked();
+        }
     }
 
     private void refreshControlsLocked() {
@@ -264,9 +266,11 @@ public final class AxKernelManagerService {
         }
     }
 
-    private synchronized ArrayList<KernelControlNode> fetchControlsList() {
-        refreshControlsLocked();
-        return new ArrayList<>(mControls.values());
+    private ArrayList<KernelControlNode> fetchControlsList() {
+        synchronized (mLock) {
+            refreshControlsLocked();
+            return new ArrayList<>(mControls.values());
+        }
     }
 
     private void publishMetadata(ArrayList<KernelControlNode> controls) {
